WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500
Thanks for tuning in to Planetarian Daily, episode 119, it's July 13th, 2026.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.640
Let's see what the latest research is telling us.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.300
A superconducting circuit now hosts the first cyclic quantum heat engine,

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:21.020
opening routes to larger quantum systems. Researchers are now altering chemical tags on DNA

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:26.380
and chromatin to control gene activity without changing the underlying sequence.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:31.900
The techniques target specific marks that influence transcription rates across cell types.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:37.300
Early applications show precise tuning of expression levels that persist through cell

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:43.440
divisions. Follow-up work will test durability and off-target effects in more complex tissues.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:49.300
From direct gene regulation to recovering hidden cell type signals in existing data,

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:56.360
next we look at a new deconvolution method. Deep details performs cross-modality deconvolution

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:01.740
on bulk sequencing data to reconstruct cell type specific regulatory processes.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:07.620
The method integrates multiple data layers to separate signals that normally blend together

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:13.520
in standard essays. It supplies higher resolution views of gene regulation without requiring

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:19.320
single cell isolation for every experiment. Researchers can now apply the approach to

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:24.820
existing bulk data sets to extract cell specific patterns that were previously inaccessible.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:31.120
Weitzmann Institute researchers combine biosynthetic pathways for five mind-altering substances

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:37.740
into a single organism. The compounds normally occur across distant branches of the tree of life.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:43.100
The engineered plant assembles the full set through coordinated metabolic steps.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:48.600
Future work will examine yields and stability of the multi-compound production system.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:54.460
The project demonstrates that pathways from separate evolutionary lineages can be coordinated

00:01:54.460 --> 00:02:01.720
within one genome. Both stories improve resolution of cellular processes. Now consider how quantum

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:08.780
scale thermodynamics might scale similar precision to larger systems. Alto University researchers built

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:13.660
the engine inside a superconducting circuit that cycles through thermodynamic states.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:19.900
The demonstration shows how quantum thermodynamics principles can be harnessed for practical devices.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:25.560
Improved understanding of these processes is expected to support larger quantum computers.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:31.900
The work also feeds back into classical thermodynamics by clarifying quantum scale behavior.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:38.400
The Alto University quantum heat engine demonstration places thermodynamics cycling inside a

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:44.640
superconducting circuit for the first time. This concrete hardware step supplies a test bed for

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:50.260
scaling quantum systems, while also refining models of energy flow at the quantum level.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:56.840
The immediate next measurements will track efficiency limits and coherence times under repeated cycles.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:02.160
How quickly can similar circuits be adapted to perform useful computational tasks

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:09.340
beyond proof-of-concept operation? From engineered quantum systems to evolved natural behaviors,

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:14.460
citizen data recently clarified how parental care arose in harvest men.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:19.780
Citizen scientists contributed eye naturalist observations that more than doubled

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:26.100
documented cases of egg guarding in harvest men. Analysis showed maternal and paternal care

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:30.800
followed distinct evolutionary trajectories rather than one preceding the other.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:37.860
The rapid data collection completed the core data set in days. Most people assume maternal care

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:44.180
evolved first and paternal care followed later in animals. In harvest men, however, the two

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:50.080
forms of egg guarding arose along independent evolutionary routes rather than one building on the

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:56.160
other. Right now, across countless species, parental behaviors continue to diversify through

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:03.240
distinct genetic and ecological pressures rather than a single linear sequence. Citizen science observations

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:09.340
