00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:58.240
breeding windows compress under rising temperatures even though their temperature responses match

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:04.460
those of southern populations. The mismatch affects chick survival and population stability.

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:10.740
Continued monitoring will track whether adaptive shifts occur. Researchers worked with residents

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:15.720
and officials in five UK cities to create guidance for tree selection and placement.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:21.080
The approach balances human benefits with ecological needs under hotter conditions.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:27.980
Local knowledge shaped criteria that standard models often overlook. Cities can now apply the

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:34.240
framework to meet both canopy and biodiversity targets. The resulting tool supplies explicit

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:41.240
decision criteria rather than generic recommendations. Oxford and Stockholm Resilient Center Analysis

